  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "83d269bb-2581-4d63-aa1a-a733bfc82e44",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The dataset contains 522 observations although not every variable has complete data, thus indicating a small amount missing data that requires handling before further analysis. Further, we have both numerical and categorical variables. From the above summary statistics:\n",
    "\n",
    "* The average wage is approximately 3.70 with a standard deviation of 3.70, indicating moderate variability in earnings.\n",
    "* Wages range from 0.53 to 24.98, showing the presence of both low-income and high income earners.\n",
    "* The distribution is likely right-skewed, as the median (4.67) is lower than the mean, meaning a smaller group of high earners is pulling the average upward.\n",
    "* The mean value is 12.56 years, with a standard deviation of 2.76 years, showing some variation in educational attainment.\n",
    "* The median age is 12, the 25th and 75th percentiles are 12 and 14 respectively, which means that a significant proportion of people have been educated up to 12 to 14 years of age, which corresponds to secondary school or higher education at an early stage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f2d5a7a9-46d5-4e28-841e-5c499875a1dc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## **II. Handling Missing Value**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "edb6cd2a-5024-4217-8790-9e476569839b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "married                 3\n",
       "hourly_wage             8\n",
       "years_in_education      3\n",
       "years_in_employment     6\n",
       "num_dependents          5\n",
       "gender                  4\n",
       "race                   10\n",
       "dtype: int64"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 7,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#identifying the missing values\n",
    "df.isna().sum()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62db3ab5-d546-459f-bc6d-e3fc9c13c550",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The missing entries in continuous variables such as `hourly_wage`, median impute is a simple and robust approach that preserves the overall distribution while avoiding the influence of extreme values. For categorical variables such as `race`, mode impute as it is valid and maintains the structure of data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "fdd7f915-3a43-4be5-835a-9a402e071759",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#filling the missing categorical data with mode value\n",
    "\n",
    "cat_cols = ['married', 'gender', 'race']\n",
    "\n",
    "for col in cat_cols:\n",
    "    df[col]=df[col].fillna(df[col].mode().iloc[0])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "1fbc2bcc-d3b5-4053-ab98-62ba1a6bb8ca",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#filling the missing numerical data with median values.\n",
    "\n",
    "num_cols = ['hourly_wage', 'years_in_education', 'years_in_employment', 'num_dependents']\n",
    "\n",
    "for col in num_cols:\n",
    "    df[col] = df[col].fillna(df[col].median())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "07b801ec-c80d-4226-b13f-7aa55f17561b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
