  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0edd5832-08e5-4c4b-857e-374a42221756",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## **III. Visual Exploration of Key Relationships**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9f78ba78-16d8-41e4-9133-5be6c9874e51",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Through the use of graphical visualisation, we will explore and obtain visual insights on:\n",
    "* The distribution of individual continuous variable.\n",
    "* Relationship between two continuous variable.\n",
    "* The association between a categorical variable and continuous variable.\n",
    "* The relationship between more than two variables."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2853f66a-d2b5-4ea8-a29b-35b0a8350bcc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### **1. Distribution of Hourly Wage**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "239b4663-4e92-495f-b5a9-c5c01a0a268e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "sns.histplot(df['hourly_wage'], bins = 20, kde = True, color = 'purple')\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution of Hourly Wage')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Hourly Wage\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Frequency\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f25c497d-c913-4c77-8e1c-15465b9c772c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The histogram provides an overview of how hourly wages are distibuted across individuals in the dataset. The distribution appears to be **right-skewed** indicating that most of the individuals tend to earn around a typical wage level, while a smaller group earns substantially more, creating a long tail to the right. The **mean hourly wage (£5.92)** is higher than **median (£4.67)** that a subset of high earners os pulling wages upward. The **range** is wide, spanning from a minimum of **£0.53** to maximum of **£24.98**, indicating diversity in earning levels within the sample. Overall, the wage distribution highlights substantial variation among earners with most workers concentrated around the lower wages levels and a smaller number achieving higher earnings."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7c4753d0-bd46-4bd0-bdaa-d6564190d6b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### **2. Relationship between Two Continuous Variables - Years in Employment and Hourly Wage**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "29b4dc72-1b07-4e4b-a6e7-abe6889abaa0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 500x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "sns.relplot(data=df, x=\"years_in_employment\", y=\"hourly_wage\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Hourly Wage vs Years in Employment\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Years in Employment\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Hourly Wages\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "bb7b8d6f-b19a-4c8b-8ab8-e08993408b4e",
