    "df['years_in_employment'].corr(df['hourly_wage'], method='pearson').item()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "93a4f8e8-9006-4775-9fce-11964d58a421",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The above graph shows a positive upward trend (through Pearson's Correlation) but relatively weak relationship between years in employment and hourly wage. Workers with higher years of experience earn more wages, although the pattern displayed is not very strong or defined. It seems there is a noticeable cluster of individuals with only a few years of experience who earn relatively low wages, while indivuals with greater work experience display greater variation in wages, including some of higher- paying positions. Overall the visual pattern indicates that the employment experience plays a factor in increasing the earnings but not the most influential one defining the level of wages."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "99fe3bb1-5a17-42fe-8121-d017c420ecce",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
