   "source": [
    "The boxplot comparing hourly wages across gender shows clear differences between the group. The median wage is visibily higher for males than that for femailes, and the upper range of wages also appears more extended. This indicates that the male workers tend to earn higher wages overall. The spread of wages also differs between the two groups. Male wages show a wider range, including several high-earnig individuals (outliers), while female wages are more tightly concentrated around lower values. This indicates that not only males earn more on average, but there is also greater variation in wage outcomes."
