   "source": [
    "## **V. Contigency Table and Test of Independence (Chi-Square Test)**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4b67d1d1-75e1-4ec2-be90-0c53f6907a66",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We will explore the relationship between two categorical variables:\n",
    "* gender\n",
    "* married\n",
    "\n",
    "We will build a contigency table(cross-tabulation of counts), then apply Chi-Square Test of Independence to check whether marital status is associated with gender."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "5f4f7dbb-68bf-486a-8290-c9c52aa0029a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Contigency Table\n",
      "marital_status  married  not_married\n",
      "gender                              \n",
      "female              131          118\n",
      "male                190           86\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#Defining the values of marital status\n",
    "df[\"marital_status\"] = df[\"married\"].astype(int).map({1: \"married\", 0: \"not_married\"})\n",
    "\n",
    "#creating contigency table\n",
    "contigency = pd.crosstab(df['gender'], df['marital_status'])\n",
    "print(\"Contigency Table\")\n",
    "print(contigency)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "4c590328-dd74-4666-8ef6-47f1b8d844d1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "contigency.plot(kind ='bar', stacked= True, rot=0)\n",
    "plt.legend(loc='center left', bbox_to_anchor=(1, 0.5))\n",
    "plt.title(\"Gender vs Marital Status\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9473f4a1-a584-4bfd-9ebd-4d1f9845acdc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Formulating the Null and Alternative hypothesis and the significance level**\n",
    "\n",
    "H0 : There is no significant association between Gender and Marital Status.\n",
    "\n",
    "H1 : There is significant association between gender and Marital Status.\n",
    "\n",
    "Assuming 5% significance level."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "40677ebc-bd11-4357-b726-3a5367123688",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "p-value: 0.0001992052578223933\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#Chi-Square test of Independence\n",
    "chi2, p_val, dof, expected = stats.chi2_contingency(contigency)\n",
    "print(f\"p-value: {p_val}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "438af615-c667-4282-88a4-92ea1d93e445",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Conclusion:** Since the p-value<0.05, we conclude that there is significant association between Gender and Marital Status. We reject the Null hypothesis. This implies that the proportions of married individuals differ between male and female workers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4dc63801-cd1a-4299-bfd5-0fc0114960f8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
