  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eedab1e1-6d94-4f82-8a71-44ad2b746ded",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Upon comparing both the statistical table, it is observed that High Education and High Experienced Workers show higher hourly wages, with an average wage of £10.30, compared to average wage of £3.98 of Low Education and Low Experienced Workers. The wage distribution in the high-educated category is also significantly broader with a maximum up to 22.86, which shows the existence of higher-paid persons that are absent in the low-educated category. Regarding the characteristics of human capital, the median of high-education group is 16 years of education and 10 years of employment, and the median of low-education group is 12 years of education and 0 years of employment. This demonstrates that the latter group comprises mostly of those who are new to the labour market or those with very minimal work experience. Overall, the table indicates that higher education and work experience are linked to significantly higher wages, and such employees also have features that are typical of people who are older and more established, including a higher rate of marriage and longer years of work experience."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "197d853e-8a44-4a99-880d-76ac7155c38b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## **VII. Test of Difference of Means (Independent Sample t-test)**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "attachments": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f95b7930-cb15-4a19-bb0c-20df8e010eda",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To check whether wages differ between two groups, we perform independent sample t-test comparing:\n",
    "* Mean hourly wage for male workers\n",
    "* Mean hourly wage for female workers\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "0b081e2d-d543-49ef-afbb-26896c8069a2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Mean Hourly Wage (Male): 7.06286231884058\n",
      "Mean Hourly Wage (Female): 4.608353413654618\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#finding the mean hourly wage for male and female workers\n",
    "\n",
    "male_wage = df[df[\"gender\"] ==\"male\"][\"hourly_wage\"]\n",
    "female_wage = df[df[\"gender\"] ==\"female\"][\"hourly_wage\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Mean Hourly Wage (Male):\", male_wage.mean())\n",
    "print(\"Mean Hourly Wage (Female):\", female_wage.mean())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9724f100-dea8-49e9-b230-3d9c55dd4768",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Formulating Null and Alternative Hypothesis and Significance level**\n",
    "\n",
    "H0: There is no difference between the means of the two populations.\n",
    "\n",
    "H1: There is significant difference between the means of the two populations.\n",
    "\n",
    "Assuming 5% significance level."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "4365ca58-2dc7-457a-b1ab-96c03f20d998",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "Independent Sample t-test results:\n",
      "t-statistic: 8.301\n",
      "p-value: 0.00000\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "t_stat, p_val = stats.ttest_ind(male_wage, female_wage, equal_var=False)\n",
    "print(\"\\nIndependent Sample t-test results:\")\n",
    "print(f\"t-statistic: {t_stat:.3f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"p-value: {p_val:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5a08574d-d429-4aba-8870-8a187d5a9dd7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Conclusion:** The sample mean shows that male workers earn higher hourly wages than female workers. The Independent sample t-test yeilds a large t-statistic and a minor p-value( less than 0.05). Therefore we reject the null hypothesis. This implies that there is presence of gender wage gap in the sample."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "17baa85d-5af1-45a2-b230-aab8d9b3081b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
